---
import {ArrowRight,Mail} from 'lucide-react';
import ReadingHeader from './ReadingHeader.astro';
const essentials=[{title:'Drawing revision',text:'3D model and 2D drawing when needed, part number, units and revision.',href:'#drawing-package'},{title:'Material & finish',text:'Exact material or functional requirement, finish details and applicable standards.',href:'#material-finish'},{title:'Acceptance criteria',text:'Critical dimensions, datums, tolerances and inspection requirements.',href:'#acceptance'},{title:'Quantity',text:'Initial quantity and expected repeat pattern.',href:'#commercial-brief'},{title:'Delivery',text:'Arrival date, packaging, shipping basis and relevant customs requirements.',href:'#commercial-brief'}];
const delivery=[['Initial quantity','Quantity per part number.'],['Repeat pattern','Expected repeat orders, if known.'],['Delivery details','Required arrival date and postcode.'],['Packaging','Any special packaging requirements.'],['Shipping basis','Incoterm and customs, duties or taxes responsibilities.'],['Response deadline','Your decision or response deadline, if applicable.']];
---
<article class="rfq-editorial reading-page">
 <ReadingHeader title="CNC machining RFQ checklist" description="Prepare the technical files and order details we need to quote your part." breadcrumbs={[{label:'Resources',href:'/resources/'},{label:'RFQ Checklist'}]}/>
 <section class="rq-wrap rq-hero reading-section" aria-labelledby="rq-essentials-title"><div class="rq-essentials"><h2 id="rq-essentials-title">Five essential requirements</h2><nav aria-label="RFQ essentials">{essentials.map(e=><a href={e.href}><h3>{e.title}</h3><p>{e.text}</p></a>)}</nav><a class="rq-download" href="/downloads/order-acceptance-checklist.txt" download>Download order acceptance checklist <ArrowRight size={18}/></a><p class="rq-note">A buyer worksheet for drawing revision, critical features, documents and shipping requirements. This is not an inspection report.</p></div></section>
 <section class="rq-wrap rq-section reading-section" aria-labelledby="rq-accepted-title"><h2 id="rq-accepted-title">Define how the part will be accepted</h2><div class="rq-columns"><section id="drawing-package"><h3>Send a consistent drawing package</h3><p>Include a 3D model, such as STEP, and a 2D drawing when dimensions, fits or surface requirements are not fully defined in the model. Label the part number, units and drawing revision. If the files disagree, identify which document controls before requesting a quotation.</p><p>For multi-axis parts, include the overall envelope, stock dimensions and part weight where known so tool access and setup can be reviewed.</p><aside class="rq-sample"><h4>Only have a sample?</h4><p>For an existing sample without a drawing, explain what is known and ask what additional measurement or design work would be needed. A sample alone cannot establish hidden material or treatment requirements.</p></aside></section><section id="acceptance"><h3>Mark the dimensions used for acceptance</h3><p>Identify mating bores and shaft fits on the drawing, with their datums and tolerances. Mark sealing faces, threads and any other critical features too. State whether dimensions apply before or after finishing.</p><p>If you need a particular inspection record, send the format or an example with your inquiry. Agree on inspection and documentation requirements before ordering, and ask LZZ to confirm the measurement method, instrument range, calibration evidence and availability of any project-specific records required for your part.</p><a class="rq-link" href="/quality/">Inspection &amp; documentation requirements <ArrowRight size={18}/></a></section></div></section>
 <section class="rq-band reading-section" id="material-finish"><div class="rq-wrap rq-section"><h2>Specify the material and final surface</h2><div class="rq-columns"><div><h3>Material requirements</h3><p>State the exact alloy or polymer grade, or the functional requirement if selection is still open. Include any required material documentation and whether substitutes may be considered.</p></div><div><h3>Finish and surface requirements</h3><p>Provide the finish specification, appearance, cosmetic faces, masking and edge conditions. Include any customer or industry standards and certificates required for this part or program. State the required standard, revision and scope.</p></div></div><p class="rq-compliance">A material or capability category on this site does not establish industry certification or application compliance. The <a href="/resources/material-and-finish-checklist/">material and finish checklist</a> explains the decisions behind these fields.</p></div></section>
 <section class="rq-wrap rq-section rq-review reading-section" id="drawing-review"><h2>What drawing review returns</h2><p>Our quotation brings together the proposed process, material, finishing, order quantity, inspection documents, production schedule and shipping basis. Where geometry or acceptance requirements need clarification, we identify the open points before you approve production.</p></section>
 <section class="rq-wrap rq-section rq-commercial reading-section" id="commercial-brief"><h2>Set the commercial brief</h2><div class="rq-commercial-grid"><div class="rq-terms"><dl><dt>Minimum order</dt><dd>1 piece</dd></dl><div><dl><dt>Production lead time</dt><dd>7–14 business days</dd></dl><p>After drawing and order confirmation, including surface finishing.<br/>Transit time is additional.</p></div></div><div class="rq-delivery"><dl>{delivery.map(([label,value])=><div><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{value}</dd></div>)}</dl></div></div></section>
 <section class="rq-wrap rq-related reading-related"><div><h2>Related part examples</h2><p>Fittings need defined threads and sealing faces; housings need mating datums and cavity details. These examples show the drawing questions for each.</p></div><div><a class="rq-link" href="/products/custom-oem-cnc-turned-fittings-connectors-and-flanges-manufacturer/">Turned fittings, connectors &amp; flanges <ArrowRight size={18}/></a><a class="rq-link" href="/products/small-batch-cnc-machining-manufacturer-complex-aluminum-housings/">Complex aluminum housings <ArrowRight size={18}/></a></div></section>
 <section class="rq-band reading-closing" id="prepare-email"><div class="rq-wrap rq-send"><div><h2>Ready to prepare the email?</h2><p>If your project needs an NDA or a controlled transfer method, contact LZZ before sending restricted files. This website does not automatically create an NDA.</p></div><div><ol><li>Prepare the draft on the inquiry page.</li><li>Attach drawings in your email application.</li><li>Review the recipients and send when ready.</li></ol><p>The inquiry page prepares an email draft locally. The website does not upload drawings or send your request.</p><a class="rq-button" href="/quote/">Prepare RFQ email <ArrowRight size={18}/></a><a class="rq-mail" href="mailto:roger@lzz-cnc.com"><Mail size={18}/>roger@lzz-cnc.com</a></div></div></section>
</article>
